[8] Two creative proof angles extracted
  angle A: blindness-pair proof
    For every scalar or low-payload carrier, pair it with the carrier that restores
    exactly the coordinate it destroys.  Examples: mu^2/phi pairs with Ramanujan/CRT
    for prime powers; automata pair with exact Farey scale plus arc-Cech/owner;
    observer cuts pair with formal exits plus exact scale.  The proof target is a
    no-unpaid-forgetting lemma.
  angle B: resonance-portfolio proof
    Work with minimal portfolios per obligation instead of one master quotient.
    The covering family, q=23 square, automatic fibers, and F7/K33 debt each need
    a different three- or four-carrier packet.  Glue them by the formal exit ledger,
    not by forcing all rows through one scalar invariant.

